//! Households, part 1 (ADR-0018 sections 4 and 7, design note of the households): where
//! people live from `Start`, birth, partnership, separation and leaving home, who cares for
//! a dependent child and who takes over when the carer dies.
//!
//! The expected bytes come from `tools/state_reference.py`, which runs the model of
//! `tools/world_reference.py`, written from the design note and not from this code.
//!
//! Scenario "homes": seed 0xff, founder tag `test:homes`, the switch off, the test data of
//! "clan" (accident 0.02 per year, the old fertility window) with the separation rate 0.01
//! per year, seven founders with reference alleles only: sim 1 (woman, 20) in a couple with
//! sim 3 (man, 22), sim 2 (woman, 21) with sim 7 (man, 23), sim 4 (man, 30) and sim 6
//! (woman, 25) single, sim 5 (boy, 12) alone. In 24 years: both couples have children;
//! sim 5 gets a household of his own at the start and leaves home at 20; partnership 2
//! separates in year 12 and her seven children stay with her; the input
//! `ArrangePartnership` pairs sim 9 (16) with sim 5 in year 17, both move into a new
//! household and her day of leaving home is cancelled; sim 11 leaves home at 18; sim 1 dies
//! in year 22 and the father in the household becomes the carer of her dependent children.
//!
//! Scenario "homes_orphans": the founders and couples of "homes" without the input, the
//! separation rate 0.05 (the test data of "split"). Partnership 1 separates in year 6, so
//! sim 1 lives alone with her children when she dies in year 22: her two dependent children
//! have no fit carer in her household and move together into a household of their own,
//! without a carer (the last stage of the orphan rule, section 6 of the note).

